      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effect of 30 min of myocardial ischemia on cardiac glycogenolysis and lactate accumulation was investigated in streptozotocin (STZ) diabetic and normal rats. In normal rats, ischemia caused a significant reduction in cardiac glycogen and a significant increase in cardiac lactate. STZ rats experienced a similar, but larger, reduction in cardiac glycogen with ischemia but did not accumulate significant quantities of lactic acid suggesting that diabetic rats have a reduced capacity for non-oxidative carbohydrate metabolism in myocardial ischemia."},
